    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72659.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 3,
    "turn_text": "Sure, I represent the 33rd Assembly District. That's the northern half of San Bernardino County. It's very rural. I have the second largest assembly district in the state, so I represent almost 10,000 square miles of rural California, seven different cities. I have a lot of mountains and a lot of desert in my district. But like many other parts of the state, my district has been hit very hard by the COVID crisis. We have not had a lot of cases, but we're still struggling to reopen. And the county is still trying to figure out how to comply with the state's requirements on going to stage two B of the reopening plan. We're having trouble with testing. The county, my district is just so spread out. It's really difficult to get testing resources to the places that they're needed.",
