  {
    "episode_id": 72659,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72659.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 9,
    "turn_text": "Sure. Well, like many of my colleagues, I found myself more busy staying at home than I normally would be traveling around the district. Now, traveling around the district, it's unusual for us to have four or five events a day, but sheltering in place from at home, I found myself with a dozen events a day, just because so many of my constituents were interested in communicating with their elected representation. So many people had concerns that they need to address. And then the workload for our district office staff has been enormous because so many people are hurting. They need to be connected to unemployment resources through the EDD or the SBA loan programs liaising with our federal representation. So all of that has been tremendously impactful.",
