  {
    "episode_id": 72659,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72659.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 17,
    "turn_text": "Well, so this will be held on Tuesday. It's a very unusual occurrence, hasn't been done in quite some time. However, what it does is allows us as a body to conduct a hearing that is, like a committee hearing, allows us to pose questions of witnesses, which normally is your wear is not done in floor sessions, but also allows all of the members of the assembly to be there at once. And the reason why We're thinking that that's required is the short, very short calendar limits on our ability to deliver a budget by the middle of June. So we want to make sure that we give our members an opportunity to ask the questions that they need to ask. So that's going to be Tuesday at one o'clock. The procedure is going to be that we have to convene. the assembly in a regular four session and then there'll be a procedural motion that requires a two-thirds affirmative vote for us to go into a committee of the whole and then that committee hearing will progress very similar to a committee hearing with questions from and statements from our members so because this is related to the budget chairman ting will preside over the assembly because i'm the vice chairman i will be i will be vice chairman of the gathering And we'll each give an opening statement, and then we'll have presentations from the Department of Finance and the Legislative Analyst, and then open it up to questions and statements from our members. And so we think that it's probably going to take about, oh, two or three hours that we'll be in session. That'll be on Tuesday.",
